+| S22 | 140-141 | Index zero via `#indexZero` | Dispatch is correct; S28 mis-models Python code-point indexing for non-ASCII. |
+| S23 | 142-143 | Slice `[1:]` via `#tail` | Dispatch is correct; S29 mis-models Python code-point slicing for non-ASCII. |
+| S24 | 144-146 | Slice `[::-1]` via `#reversed` | Dispatch is correct; S30/S32-S33 reverse bytes, not Python code points. |
+| S25 | 147-148 | Direct-name one-argument call | Correct for the fixed module and evaluated argument. |
+| S26 | 155 | Integer negation primitive | Correct. |
+| S27 | 156 | String concatenation primitive | Correct for the represented K byte strings. |
+| S28 | 157-158 | `string[0]` as `substrString(S,0,1)` | Materially false as a Python bridge on UTF-8-encoded non-ASCII inputs. |
+| S29 | 159-160 | `string[1:]` as byte substring | Materially false as a Python bridge on non-ASCII inputs. |
