+Concrete false witness for S28-S33: the valid Python input `"é"` returns
+`"é"` from both trusted and generated Python. With the translator-compatible
+K input literal `"\u00e9"`, fresh `EXECUTION` produces bytes
+`c3 a9 c3`, shown in `stage3-concrete-semantics-comparison-final2.log`.
+For `"λ漢🙂"`, the K configuration path is rejected for the JSON surrogate
+escape, and direct UTF-8 input reverses bytes into an invalid UTF-8 result.
+
+## `verification.k` rules
+
+| ID | Lines | Exact role | Static finding |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| V01 | 10-11 | Dispatches `#reference(S)` on `S ==String #reverse(S)` | A byte-string recursion, not independently proved to express the HumanEval property. |
+| V02 | 12-13 | Palindromic/true choice returns `S` | Correct on the guard. |
+| V03 | 14-18 | False choice mirrors the first byte around recursive tail | Guards are disjoint from V02 and recursion decreases byte length. The `[total]` declaration is globally over-broad at `#referenceChoice("",false)`, though that ground case is unreachable from V01. |
+| V04 | 24-27 | Priority operational bridge: exact `make_palindrome` call on `P ==K #solution` rewrites directly to `strVal(#reference(S))` | Illegitimate target-conclusion axiom. It skips S04-S33; no bridge-free universal connection claim exists. Removing it leaves the universal claim stuck. A constructor-level body mutation to `return "broken"` leaves the claim at `#Top`, while fixed execution returns `"broken"` and bridge-enabled execution returns `"catac"` for `"cat"`. |
+| V05 | 32 | Defines `#isPalindrome(S)` as byte-string equality with `#reverse(S)` | Truthful only for the generated byte-string model, not Python Unicode semantics. |
+
+V04 reads the already evaluated `strVal(S)` and exact module `P`; in this
+minimal semantics it skips no heap/output cells because none exist. It
+nevertheless replaces the entire program-defined lookup, binding, body,
